WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.610
- Tattoo artist Kat Von D is in hot water

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.540
for potentially stealing
someone's photograph

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:05.960
to use it in a tattoo.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.300
This has a lot of people confused.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.730
It seems like a tattoo
is a transformative work.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.820
And how is that like
the actual photograph?

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:12.653
Well, first of all,

00:00:12.653 --> 00:00:14.250
photographs can obviously be copyrighted,

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.650
and the fact that it's transformative

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.483
isn't really the issue.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.250
That actually might
hurt more than it helps.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.520
Just because you've changed the medium

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.110
and taken it from a photograph
and turned it into a tattoo

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.280
doesn't mean that you haven't committed

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.130
copyright infringement.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.020
In fact, that's probably
a derivative work.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.680
Imagine if you took a
book like "Jurassic Park"

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.400
and turned it into the
movie "Jurassic Park."

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.233
You've changed the medium,

00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:33.600
but you're still infringing
on the copyright.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.720
And fair use probably doesn't apply

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.100
because you're not changing the purpose

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.270
of the original photograph,

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.110
it's still being viewed for,
effectively, entertainment.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.610
So Kat Von D could be in hot water

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.390
and liable for hundreds
of thousands of dollars

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:44.910
under statutory damages.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.300
Which is why she should
really watch this channel

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.553
because if you don't,
I'll see you in court.

